    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001>
        <Title>kafedra-flow-intake: fix active/archive view and stale-detail states</Title>
        <DependsOn></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Lifecycle mode changes through one explicit action and never changes persisted plan status.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Search and ordinary filters remain; an absent selected plan never remains in the detail pane.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Loading, no-result, archive/restore and repeated-switch states remain deterministic.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/lifecycle.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>kafedra-design: specify persistent segmented hierarchy without a mobile-specific mode</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-001 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The lifecycle segment is permanently visible before ordinary filters and not duplicated by a visible select.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Text, shape, aria-selected and focus express selection independently of color.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The 1440x900 primary desktop geometry, narrowed desktop window and 44 pixel targets are fixed and never-learn.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>kafedra-motion: use a restrained interruptible selection transition</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-002 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Only background, border, shadow or indicator state transitions for 120–180 milliseconds.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Reduced motion is instant and data loading, focus and keyboard actions never wait for animation.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>No mobile navigation or mobile-specific transition is added.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-003>
      <T-004>
        <Title>kafedra-feature: add an accessible adapter over the existing lifecycle state bridge</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-003 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The adapter hides the legacy select, emits its existing change event and performs no direct API filtering.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Click, Enter, Space and arrow-key interaction update the correct status-filtered server request.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Mode-specific empty text is applied only after the existing plans loader reports a no-result state.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/plans-lifecycle-segment.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-004>
      <T-005>
        <Title>kafedra-design-audit: inspect actual focus, desktop overflow and reduced-motion states</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-004 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The audit records PASS, REVISE or BLOCK for primary desktop, narrowed desktop, keyboard, focus, empty and reduced-motion behavior.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The audit explicitly confirms that no distinct mobile mode or mobile state machine was introduced.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>No blocker or major issue remains before final tests.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-005>
      <T-006>
        <Title>kafedra-tests: prove one-action server filtering and compatibility</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-005 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Unit tests cover stable modes, keyboard calculation, single state bridge, 44 pixel target and reduced motion.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Playwright desktop covers 1440x900 and a narrowed 900x700 window, click, keyboard, server query, preserved search, stale detail, empty state and page overflow.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Existing lifecycle tests continue to pass through the hidden compatibility select; no new mobile-specific test or behavior is added.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm test</Command><Command>npx playwright test tests/browser/plans-lifecycle-segment.spec.mjs --project=desktop</Command></Verification>
      </T-006>
      <T-007>
        <Title>kafedra-release: exact-head merge, post-merge and terminal archive</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-006 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>GRACE final and every required project check succeed on one unchanged PR head.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Squash merge is followed by successful post-merge CI before a separate archive-only applied transition.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Issue 252 closes only after the terminal lifecycle is confirmed.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run check</Command><Command>npm run docs:check</Command><Command>npm test</Command></Verification>
      </T-007>
